Usage: reset [options] [terminal]

Reset terminal to its default state.

OPTIONS:
  -I             no initialization strings
  -c             set control characters
  -e ARG         erase character
  -i ARG         interrupt character
  -k ARG         kill character
  -m ARG         map identifier to type
  -q             display term only, do no changes
  -Q             do not output control key settings
  -r             display term on stderr
  -s             output TERM set command
  -V             print curses-version
  -w             set window-size
      --help     display this help and exit
      --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
